# Spam URLs flagged in GSC coverage report (PMAC - #136) - return 410 Gone.
# Place near the top of .htaccess, before the WordPress rewrite block.
#
# The vast majority of flagged URLs are two injected patterns:
#   /dp/<hex-id>            e.g. /dp/002520756, /dp/1a2138749
#   /cate-<n> or /cate-<n>-<n>  (also the odd /cate--<n> double-dash form)
# Rather than list every one of the 900+ individual IDs (which will keep
# growing as the injection keeps generating new ones), these two are matched
# by pattern so any current or future URL in the same format is covered.
# The remaining flagged URLs don't follow a shared pattern and are listed
# individually below.

# All RedirectMatch rules below return HTTP 410 Gone
# --- Pattern-matched spam (bulk of the list) ---
RedirectMatch 410 ^/dp/[0-9a-f]+/?$
RedirectMatch 410 ^/cate-{1,2}[0-9]+(-[0-9]+)?/?$

# --- Individually flagged spam pages (casino/gambling injected content) ---
